= V1 page-role migration =

The first corpus inventory established that V1 mixed several different jobs inside the Main namespace: subject knowledge, BITwiki architecture, reusable fragments, navigation, validation machinery, and historical variants.

This page performs the next maturation step:

<blockquote>'''Classify the artifact before classifying the thing it talks about.'''</blockquote>

A MediaWiki page is not automatically a first-class knowledge object. A page may instead be a reusable section, index, specification, constitutional source, interface surface, maintenance artifact, or historical branch.

The complete machine-readable matrix is generated by <code>scripts/classify_v1_page_roles.py</code> after <code>scripts/inventory_corpus.py</code>.

== Migration role is not ontology ==

The role vocabulary on this page exists only to answer what job a historical artifact performs during migration.

It must not become a new <code>Entity type</code> vocabulary.

{| class="wikitable"
! Migration role !! Job
|-
| <code>canonical_subject_candidate</code> || First-class real-world subject/project object that may directly pressure V2 Entity type and Domain vocabulary.
|-
| <code>architecture_system_source</code> || BITwiki/BITCORE architecture, schema, ontology, epistemics, governance, constitutional, documentation, or system-design source.
|-
| <code>book_matter_reusable</code> || Reusable section, fragment, or subpage whose content may seed canonical knowledge but whose historical artifact role is compositional.
|-
| <code>navigation_interface</code> || Index, list, landing, notice, or orientation surface.
|-
| <code>maintenance_validation_test</code> || Operational audit, test, validation implementation, or maintenance artifact.
|-
| <code>unresolved</code> || Insufficient evidence for a high-confidence role assignment.
|}

Lifecycle is orthogonal. A page may be an architecture source and also a historical variant. A navigation surface may also be an alternate presentation. Role and lineage must not be compressed into one label.

