== Architecture and system sources ==

The largest family contains 83 pages.

This includes V1's strongest ontology, epistemics, schema, constitutional, governance, template, SMW, provenance, interoperability, quality, deployment, and technical writings.

These pages should not be thrown away because they are "meta." They are among the most important V1 sources for understanding what BITwiki was attempting to become.

Their migration path is different from subject articles:

<pre>
preserve exact source + revisions
        ↓
reconcile parallel branches
        ↓
identify durable design signal
        ↓
map to current V2 architecture
        ↓
retain historical alternatives where intellectually meaningful
        ↓
canonicalize only the present architectural contract
</pre>

This family is where manifesto/charter voice, ontology experiments, confidence systems, schema proposals, template architecture, and research-system ambition should be mined rather than flattened.

== Navigation and interface sources ==

Nineteen pages are primarily navigation/interface artifacts: indices, lists, Main Page variants, Start Here / How to Navigate surfaces, Site notice, and related orientation material.

Their existence supports a plural navigation model:

* curated landing pages;
* indices and lists;
* Portals;
* Categories;
* semantic query views;
* compatibility/navigation redirects;
* machine-readable maps.

They should pressure [[BITwiki:Navigation]], not the subject ontology.

== Maintenance, validation, and test artifacts ==

Six pages are explicitly operational/test artifacts:

* <code>PHASE3 DEPLOYMENT AUDIT</code>;
* <code>Template Improvement Recommendations</code>;
* <code>Template Validation Implementation</code>;
* <code>Template Validation Lua Module</code>;
* <code>Template Validation Report</code>;
* <code>Test Page</code>.

They remain useful implementation-history evidence but should not be migrated as ordinary durable knowledge pages merely because they existed in Main.

== Lifecycle and parallel branches ==

The matrix records lifecycle flags separately from migration role.

The present snapshot contains:

* 12 pages flagged as historical variants or parallel branches;
* 5 parallel <code>Component:</code> naming surfaces;
* 1 alternate Main Page presentation;
* preserved multi-revision history on 159 pages.

Examples include <code>.REVISED</code> pages, <code>BITwiki Charter Revised</code>, <code>Main Page styled</code>, Coraline integration material, revision summaries, and parallel component naming.

These flags are not automatic deletion instructions. They identify where canonicalization must compare branches rather than silently choosing whichever title looks newest.

== Ontology pressure after role separation ==

The page-role pass substantially narrows what should directly shape the base V2 ontology.

Direct first-class subject evidence currently comes from:

# Bioluminescent Organisms;
# Fluorescent Coral Reefs;
# the twelve V2 domain exemplars;
# future canonical subject pages recovered from historical fragment signal or new reviewed corpus material.

Reusable fragments provide secondary evidence for patterns already anticipated by V2:

* Concept — definition fragments such as emergence, feedback loop, homeostasis;
* Method — systems analysis methodology;
* Protocol — peer review and validation procedures;
* evidence/epistemic structures — empirical validation and peer-review summaries.

This is evidence in favor of the current broad V2 decomposition, but it is still not sufficient to freeze the final vocabulary.

== Next maturation step ==

With page role separated from ontology, the next review can work on the two streams independently.

=== Subject canonicalization stream ===

For each first-class subject candidate and reusable subject signal:

# identify the object actually being modeled;
# compare all source revisions and composed fragments;
# recover citations and original authored depth;
# determine the primary V2 Entity type;
# determine Domain membership;
# model secondary roles through explicit relationships where cleaner;
# identify genuinely repeated missing types/properties;
# preserve uncertainty and provenance.

=== Architecture maturation stream ===

For the 83 system sources:

# group by design family;
# reconcile branches and contradictions;
# preserve strong authored language and philosophical lineage;
# distinguish intended capability from implemented capability;
# mature primitives into current V2 only where the job survives.

The two streams meet through the [[BITwiki:V1 maturation register]], but neither should be allowed to distort the other.

== Reproducibility and validation ==

Run:

<pre>
python scripts/validate_v2.py
python scripts/inventory_corpus.py
python scripts/classify_v1_page_roles.py
</pre>

The role classifier fails if the archived V1 Main count stops matching the verified 162-page snapshot or if a page cannot be assigned a high-confidence migration role. This makes new ambiguity visible instead of silently defaulting it into an ontology class.

The generated <code>v1-page-role-matrix.json</code> preserves for every page:

* page title/path/id and current revision;
* migration role;
* rationale and evidence signals;
* lifecycle flags;
* composition signal;
* API-recorded categories and identity categories;
* Infobox type source parameter;
* classification annotation source syntax.

See [[BITwiki:Corpus evidence]], [[BITwiki:V1 ontology maturation]], [[BITwiki:V1 maturation register]], [[BITwiki:Book Matter]], [[BITwiki:Transclusion]], [[BITwiki:Ontology]], and [[BITwiki:Source lineage]].

